{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:16-1","provision":"BCO 16-1","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"16-1","title":"Section 16-1","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/16-1/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/16-1","current_text":{"html":"<p>Ordinary vocation to office in the Church is the calling of God by the Spirit, through the inward testimony of a good conscience, the manifest approbation of God's people, and the concurring judgment of a lawful court of the Church.</p>","text":"Ordinary vocation to office in the Church is the calling of God by the Spirit, through the inward testimony of a good conscience, the manifest approbation of God's people, and the concurring judgment of a lawful court of the Church."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"3215b08b64db0d1ab36e0721b999ec192d812d74","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"e5fd669690c4b80754c46f09d04273adf2ccbfb6563342677c52c5cde8a91808","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12455,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12455},"parent_id":"bco:16","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":5,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Psiaki v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-567bfc2ca0da","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":108},"excerpt":"has appointed in His Church.\" BCO 16-1 reiterates this principle in holding","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minor communicant voting","congregational meeting","voting rights","good and regular standing","church bylaws","officer election","communicant membership","BCO 6-4","BCO 20-3","BCO 24-3","BCO 25-1","age restrictions","session authority"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained Psiaki’s complaint and held that the CPC Session erred by ordaining and installing officers elected at a February 5, 2023 congregational meeting where the congregation’s bylaw excluded communing members under 18 from voting. Reading BCO 6-4, 25-1, and 25-7 together, the SJC ruled that all communing members are entitled to vote and that local bylaws cannot impose an age restriction; the “good and regular standing” language addresses censure, not age. The decision did not annul the completed ordination/installation, but required future elections and installations to comply with the Constitution."}},{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Harrell et al. v. Covenant Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md:occ-fdc453c82c1f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":534},"excerpt":"of a lawful court of the Church.\" (BCO 16-1). “[T]he right of God's people","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["indictment specificity","sufficiency of indictment","BCO 32-5 times places circumstances","mission church polity","congregational right to select minister","organizing pastor election","fifth commandment","ninth commandment","disqualification of judges","standard of review in appeals","provisional Session authority","particularization of mission church","BCO 31-2 investigation","due process","mission church","particularization","congregational rights","minister selection","witnesses as judges","contumacy","location of trial","reference to presbytery","membership vows","slander","organizing pastor"],"standard_of_review":"factual_findings","review_standards":["factual_findings"],"case_numbers":["2022-7"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained an appeal by seven members of a 38-member mission church who were convicted by their temporary Session of opposing the organizing minister's expected election as pastor. Reversing the Presbytery's affirmance and the guilty verdicts underlying indefinite suspensions, the SJC held the indictments fatally lacked BCO 32-5 specificity; Presbytery used the wrong standard of review; the Session had no authority to control pastoral selection; and no Fifth or Ninth Commandment offense was proved. Challenges to witness-judges, venue, and refusal to refer were rejected."}},{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Dodson et al. v. Ohio Presbytery","year":2021,"disposition":"other","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.md:occ-0f9091c11b4a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":399},"excerpt":"[^fn-ga48-p683-n2]:See also BCO 16-1, 19-16.c, 37-3, 37-4, 37-5 and 42-12.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-01.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["heresy","Trinity","partialism","excommunication","contumacy","censures","indefinite suspension","order of censures","BCO 27-5","BCO 30-4","personal offenses vs. general offenses","lay member discipline","evidence of contumacy"],"standard_of_review":"mixed","review_standards":["factual_findings","discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2019-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Grace PCA’s Session challenged Ohio Presbytery’s reversal of excommunication for two members convicted of heresy. The SJC partially sustained the complaint: prior indefinite suspension was not constitutionally required, but Presbytery properly found excommunication too severe because the trial record contained no evidence of contumacy. Presbytery nevertheless had to impose an appropriate lesser censure or remand for one, and lacked authority to mandate transfer to another church. The unappealed heresy convictions remained, but because the members had joined another church, further proceedings were moot."}},{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Thornton v. Westminster Presbytery","year":2006,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md:occ-50bd92d7eefa","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":86},"excerpt":"The administrative remedy of BCO 34-10 arises from BCO 16-1 and","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md"},{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md:occ-7d75f207d0d7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":87},"excerpt":"Preliminary Principle 6. BCO 16-1 states that calling to ecclesiastical office","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md"},{"id":"bco:16-1--case:cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md:occ-44f222f5862d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":99},"excerpt":"presbytery, where the third necessary affirmation of BCO 16-1 is lacking –","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga34_2006__2004-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["pastoral call approval","presbytery discretion","divestiture without censure","BCO 34-10 administrative remedy","congregation right to elect pastor","BCO 20-10 vs 21-1","Preliminary Principle 6","minister without call"],"standard_of_review":"discretion_and_judgment","review_standards":["discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2004-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Thornton challenged Westminster Presbytery’s refusal to place Memorial PCA Session’s call in his hands and its simultaneous initiation of administrative divestiture without censure. The SJC sustained both issues, reversed the divestiture decision, and remanded with directions to approve and deliver the call and set an installation date. A valid call supplied the congregational approbation whose absence BCO 34-10’s administrative remedy requires; Presbytery also could not rely on undisclosed concerns while avoiding required judicial process. The ruling found clear error, not an absence of all presbyterial review authority."}},{"id":"bco:16-1--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/potomac__009.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/potomac__009.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Potomac: ( BCO 3-1, BCO 13-9, BCO 16-1 and BCO 25-8 through 11) – Presbytery appointed a commission","year":2011,"disposition":"raised","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/potomac__009.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/potomac__009.html","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:16-1--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/potomac__009.html:occ-431579999f28","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/potomac__009.html","repository_path":"rpr/exc/potomac__009.html","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/rpr_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/potomac__009.html"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}}],"history":[]}
